    {
      "name": "fonts",
      "type": "registry:file",
      "title": "Self-hosted Brand Fonts",
      "description": "@font-face rules for Bai Jamjuree, which only goes 20px and up and never sets a number, and Inter variable, which does all the UI and data with tabular figures. Nothing is loaded off Google's servers, because a FIVIC app never calls out to anyone else while it's running. Comes with a script you run once at setup that pulls the woff2 files into public/fonts/. Both families are SIL Open Font License 1.1.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/fivic/fonts.css",
          "type": "registry:file",
          "target": "src/fonts/fonts.css"
        },
        {
          "path": "scripts/fetch-fonts.mjs",
          "type": "registry:file",
          "target": "scripts/fetch-fonts.mjs"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "agents",
      "type": "registry:file",
      "title": "Agent Conventions",
      "description": "Rules for Claude Code and Cursor working in FIVIC OS. Install from this registry, theme first, don't mix up --brand and --primary, never write a colour value in a component, numbers are always tabular, Bai Jamjuree never sets a number, 32px controls instead of 36px, both modes in one commit, and nothing calls out to another server. Put this in every app and every repo.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/rules/AGENTS.md",
          "type": "registry:file",
          "target": "~/AGENTS.md"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "logo",
      "type": "registry:component",
      "title": "Brand Mark",
      "description": "The fivic mark as a React component. It draws from currentColor, so one component covers brand teal on light, white on dark, and muted when something's turned off. FivicMark for the raw shape, FivicLogo for the mark at --brand. The full lockup with the wordmark isn't in here, that needs fivic's vector artwork, which we haven't got yet.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/fivic/logo.tsx",
          "type": "registry:component",
          "target": "components/brand/logo.tsx"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "button",
      "type": "registry:ui",
      "title": "Button",
      "description": "The FIVIC button. 32px by default instead of shadcn's 36px, because up and down space is the scarcest thing on these screens. The filled one uses --primary, and there's deliberately no brand variant, because white on the logo teal fails WCAG AA. Sizes are sm (28px, inline and in table rows), default (32px), and lg (36px, for the one main action on a page). The label is text-label at all three: size changes the control, not the type.",
      "dependencies": [
        "@radix-ui/react-slot",
        "class-variance-authority"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/fivic/button.tsx",
          "type": "registry:ui",
          "target": "components/ui/button.tsx"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "status-chip",
      "type": "registry:ui",
      "title": "Status Chip",
      "description": "The one place state gets named and coloured in FIVIC OS. Almost every list row carries a state, and without a single component the same state ends up named three ways and coloured four. Tones are success (settled), warning (needs a person to look at it), danger (rejected or failed), info (the system did it, nobody's confirmed it yet), and neutral. Measured at 4.5:1 or better in both modes.",
      "dependencies": [
        "class-variance-authority"
      ],
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "registry/fivic/status-chip.tsx",
          "type": "registry:ui",
          "target": "components/ui/status-chip.tsx"
        }
      ]
    }
